From: Cristian Magherusan-Stanciu <cristi@leanercloud.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:04:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] connection: keep the event handler alive while it runs

A handler that replaces itself with xpc_connection_set_event_handler from
inside the callback (the usual way to break its own retain cycle, seen on
XPC_ERROR_CONNECTION_INVALID) released the block that was still executing,
so everything it captured was destroyed before the handler body finished.
Invoke every event through call_event_handler, which holds the block for the
duration of the call.

Add libxpc_test_handler_lifetime: a client object whose dealloc requires a
prior invalidate is captured by the handler of a connection to a missing
service; the handler replaces itself and then invalidates the client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2LBeE7Q2BrLby6CJ5eL7p
